00:27:43.390 --> 00:27:45.944
Humu mimi nitakamata tani.


00:27:47.531 --> 00:27:49.326
Humu mimi kuwa tani.


00:29:21.178 --> 00:29:23.939
<i>Humu mimi nitakamata tani.</i>


00:29:23.939 --> 00:29:26.423
<i>Humu mimi kuwa tani.</i>


00:29:28.598 --> 00:29:30.773
He was called in
missing about one a.m.


00:29:30.773 --> 00:29:32.913
Some kids found him here.


00:29:32.913 --> 00:29:36.088
Wife said, he goes out
fishing, but never out past 10:00.


00:29:36.088 --> 00:29:37.746
My guess is that he
came upon something


00:29:37.746 --> 00:29:39.092
he wasn't supposed to see.


00:29:39.092 --> 00:29:40.541
Yeah. Anything else?


00:29:40.541 --> 00:29:41.991
Oh, yeah. There's more.


00:29:41.991 --> 00:29:43.441
You're gonna wanna see this.


00:29:50.759 --> 00:29:53.624
<i>Mimi nitakamata tani.</i>


00:29:53.624 --> 00:29:55.590
<i>Humu mimi kuwa tani.</i>


00:29:56.489 --> 00:29:57.662
What do we got, Nick?


00:29:57.662 --> 00:30:00.009
Hispanic male,
about 10 years old.


00:30:00.009 --> 00:30:02.633
Looks exactly like what we
saw at the river yesterday.


00:30:02.633 --> 00:30:03.667
Shit.


00:30:42.292 --> 00:30:43.846
Nick, make sure I get
a picture of that, please.


00:30:43.846 --> 00:30:44.882
Okay.


00:30:50.267 --> 00:30:51.819
<i>The old man would've died anyway</i>


00:30:51.819 --> 00:30:53.752
from his throat being cut,


00:30:53.752 --> 00:30:56.480
if he'd had a heart left
to pump the blood out.


00:30:56.859 --> 00:30:57.894
What?


00:30:57.894 --> 00:30:59.932
His heart had been
sliced out clean,


00:30:59.932 --> 00:31:02.347
and there was no
blood in his throat.


00:31:02.347 --> 00:31:05.489
So whoever did this,
it was awfully quick.


00:31:05.489 --> 00:31:07.386
I mean, when you say
quick, like, how quick?


00:31:07.386 --> 00:31:09.458
I mean, like his heart
might've still been beating.


00:31:09.458 --> 00:31:10.942
But what about the
heart? Did you find it?


00:31:10.942 --> 00:31:12.151
No.


00:31:12.151 --> 00:31:13.669
No?
- No. Didn't find it.


00:31:15.775 --> 00:31:17.741
What about the boy?


00:31:17.741 --> 00:31:19.778
Well, the boy was
like the first girl.


00:31:19.778 --> 00:31:21.538
- Yeah?
- Mutilated.


00:31:21.538 --> 00:31:24.957
Parts cut off. Missing.


00:31:24.957 --> 00:31:29.029
One thing. Whatever
this guy is using,


00:31:29.029 --> 00:31:30.307
is sharp as hell.


00:31:30.307 --> 00:31:31.859
Okay.


00:31:31.859 --> 00:31:33.619
Want a little snoot?


00:31:33.619 --> 00:31:34.932
Got some good whiskey here.


00:31:34.932 --> 00:31:36.209
Yeah, I'll take a little snoot.


00:31:37.038 --> 00:31:38.279
And there's another, uh...


00:31:39.177 --> 00:31:40.730
another thing interesting.


00:31:40.730 --> 00:31:41.973
Yeah?


00:31:41.973 --> 00:31:44.561
Remember those things
you brought from the altar?


00:31:44.561 --> 00:31:45.769
Yes, sir.


00:31:46.701 --> 00:31:47.980
Well...


00:31:50.809 --> 00:31:51.845
Cheers.


00:31:55.538 --> 00:31:56.780
This one...


00:31:59.198 --> 00:32:00.992
It's finely powdered gold.


00:32:02.304 --> 00:32:03.374
What do you mean, gold?


00:32:03.374 --> 00:32:05.583
Like Fort Knox Gold.


00:32:06.204 --> 00:32:07.171
No shit.


00:32:08.482 --> 00:32:09.518
And these...


00:32:11.141 --> 00:32:13.590
These are some - herbs you brought.
- Yeah?


00:32:13.590 --> 00:32:15.662
I've been able to ID one of 'em.


00:32:16.525 --> 00:32:18.250
And it's, uh,


00:32:18.250 --> 00:32:19.838
something called rooibos.


00:32:20.321 --> 00:32:22.185
What's that?


00:32:22.185 --> 00:32:23.980
Well, there's been
some research on it.


00:32:23.980 --> 00:32:26.569
It's from Africa.
It's a red tea.


00:32:26.569 --> 00:32:28.674
Mmm. It ain't that
kinda tea though.


00:32:30.262 --> 00:32:31.298
Thanks, Bill.


00:32:31.298 --> 00:32:32.507
Not like you drink.


00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:55.011
Shit. Excuse me.


00:32:55.011 --> 00:32:56.738
Do you know where
Dr. Mackles' office is?


00:32:56.738 --> 00:32:58.257
- That way.
- It's back this way?


00:32:58.257 --> 00:32:59.258
- Yeah.
- Gosh.


00:33:16.516 --> 00:33:17.690
Come in.


00:33:22.143 --> 00:33:23.936
May I help you?


00:33:23.936 --> 00:33:25.008
Well, I hope so.


00:33:26.526 --> 00:33:27.700
Are you Dr. Mackles?


00:33:28.114 --> 00:33:29.183
Yes.


00:33:29.183 --> 00:33:30.943
I'm homicide
detective Lucas Boyd.


00:33:32.567 --> 00:33:33.602
Do you mind if I sit?


00:33:36.432 --> 00:33:39.815
So, you teach African
studies, is that right?


00:33:39.815 --> 00:33:41.438
Yes.


00:33:42.439 --> 00:33:43.577
Are you from Africa?


00:33:44.474 --> 00:33:46.442
Yes. Lesotho.


00:33:47.512 --> 00:33:49.272
Where is that at?


00:33:49.272 --> 00:33:51.826
It's a small country in
the heart of South Africa.


00:33:51.826 --> 00:33:52.863
Oh.


00:33:53.622 --> 00:33:56.693
Is my being African important?


00:33:56.693 --> 00:33:58.351
Well, again, I hope so.


00:33:58.351 --> 00:34:00.457
Do you, uh, know
what rooibos is?


00:34:02.459 --> 00:34:04.667
Yes. It's tea.


00:34:05.220 --> 00:34:06.186
Just tea?


00:34:08.188 --> 00:34:10.742
Well, it's sometimes
used medicinally.


00:34:10.742 --> 00:34:11.813
Mmm-hmm.


00:34:17.681 --> 00:34:20.994
Um, smell this, and tell
me what it is, will you?


00:34:38.010 --> 00:34:39.081
Where did you get this?


00:34:40.876 --> 00:34:43.155
Why? What is it?


00:34:47.606 --> 00:34:50.402
Dr. Mackles. What is it?


00:34:52.128 --> 00:34:54.889
It's... herbs.


00:34:56.960 --> 00:34:58.893
Mmm-hmm. Just any kind of herbs?


00:35:00.585 --> 00:35:03.001
Well, I would say yohimbe bark


00:35:03.001 --> 00:35:08.110
and, uh, some other
fermented tree roots.


00:35:08.110 --> 00:35:09.594
Hmm.


00:35:09.594 --> 00:35:10.940
Where'd you get it?


00:35:11.942 --> 00:35:13.115
I found it at a crime scene.


00:35:21.054 --> 00:35:22.503
What kind of crime?


00:35:25.057 --> 00:35:26.681
Well, I'm a homicide
detective, sir.


00:35:37.105 --> 00:35:38.588
Can you tell me what
these writings are?


00:35:44.077 --> 00:35:46.045
You could easily
google this, Detective.


00:35:46.045 --> 00:35:48.081
I know. I know.
And I actually did.


00:35:48.081 --> 00:35:49.186
It didn't make sense to me.


00:35:50.324 --> 00:35:52.257
But then I did Google


00:35:52.257 --> 00:35:55.295
leading scholars in African
culture, and your name came up,


00:35:55.295 --> 00:35:56.780
as the best and brightest.


00:35:57.436 --> 00:35:59.920
So, here I am.


00:36:04.443 --> 00:36:07.686
I'm sorry. I cannot help you.


00:36:11.277 --> 00:36:14.969
Well, I appreciate
your time, sir.


00:37:06.297 --> 00:37:08.023
I'm just looking for someone.


00:37:09.092 --> 00:37:10.128
A ghost.


00:37:12.994 --> 00:37:14.443
I need to put a
name to this face.


00:37:17.722 --> 00:37:18.793
I've seen him around.


00:37:18.793 --> 00:37:19.896
Great.


00:37:21.139 --> 00:37:23.280
He's my main suspect
in some strange killings.


00:37:25.557 --> 00:37:26.559
We found an altar.


00:37:26.559 --> 00:37:28.353
Blood.


00:37:28.353 --> 00:37:29.838
I don't really know
what it means.


00:37:34.291 --> 00:37:35.429
He's a Sangoma.


00:37:37.570 --> 00:37:38.606
Sangoma?


00:37:39.952 --> 00:37:40.987
Touched by God.


00:37:41.643 --> 00:37:42.817
A witch doctor.


00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:44.922
He works for clients.


00:37:46.786 --> 00:37:47.856
What kind of clients?


00:37:49.927 --> 00:37:51.376
Rich and powerful ones.


00:37:54.380 --> 00:37:56.175
May I give you a word of advice?


00:37:56.795 --> 00:37:58.003
Mmm-hmm.


00:37:58.797 --> 00:38:00.041
Be careful.


00:38:01.318 --> 00:38:02.699
He could be coming for you.


00:38:13.813 --> 00:38:14.813
Thank you.


00:38:17.885 --> 00:38:18.922
Is everything okay?


00:38:45.016 --> 00:38:46.983
Dr. Mackles, I need your help.


00:38:48.054 --> 00:38:50.262
God dam it, two kids are dead.


00:38:50.262 --> 00:38:52.057
They were butchered like hogs.


00:38:53.231 --> 00:38:55.130
You know what these
writings are, don't you?


00:38:56.684 --> 00:38:57.994
Now, please,


00:38:58.927 --> 00:39:00.032
take another look.


00:39:02.724 --> 00:39:04.657
I cannot help you.


00:39:05.864 --> 00:39:06.900
Can't or won't?


00:39:16.047 --> 00:39:17.221
You're scared, aren't you?


00:39:50.081 --> 00:39:51.601
Watch your step, doctor.


00:40:06.788 --> 00:40:07.789
Oh.


00:40:14.036 --> 00:40:15.278
What is it, doctor?


00:40:16.764 --> 00:40:18.731
It's Swahili.


00:40:19.559 --> 00:40:20.836
Zulu.


00:40:20.836 --> 00:40:22.045
Hmm.


00:40:22.045 --> 00:40:23.840
It identifies territory.


00:40:24.702 --> 00:40:26.117
Identifies how?


00:40:27.050 --> 00:40:29.016
Uh, centers of power, or...


00:40:29.914 --> 00:40:32.744
ways to get access
to that power.


00:40:33.952 --> 00:40:36.646
Do me a favor. Can
you read that right there?


00:40:37.577 --> 00:40:40.512
Well, roughly.


00:40:45.688 --> 00:40:49.485
Uh, "Here I take the power.


00:40:49.485 --> 00:40:52.108
"Here I become the power."


00:40:54.284 --> 00:40:56.079
Your man is a Sangoma.


00:40:57.182 --> 00:40:59.391
A medicine man.


00:40:59.391 --> 00:41:01.567
In your culture, you would
call him a witch doctor.


00:41:04.224 --> 00:41:06.157
The way he's killing,
that makes sense.


00:41:09.092 --> 00:41:11.507
You ever hear the
term <i>"Muti,"</i> Detective?


00:41:11.887 --> 00:41:12.992
No.


00:41:14.822 --> 00:41:17.065
It's Zulu. It means medicine.


00:41:17.065 --> 00:41:19.067
But, Muti has a dark side.


00:41:21.483 --> 00:41:26.039
So, are you saying that he is
using the body parts for medicine?


00:41:26.902 --> 00:41:28.110
Exactly.


00:41:28.110 --> 00:41:29.284
- Right.
- Well,


00:41:29.284 --> 00:41:31.045
you know,
pharmaceutical companies


00:41:31.045 --> 00:41:34.876
use stem cells from aborted
fetuses to create vaccines.


00:41:34.876 --> 00:41:35.981
Right.


00:41:35.981 --> 00:41:37.500
Well, this is just
a primitive version


00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:38.983
of that concept.


00:41:38.983 --> 00:41:40.364
I'm listening.


00:41:40.364 --> 00:41:42.056
Well, in a metaphysical sense,


00:41:42.056 --> 00:41:45.922
<i>it can be tied to what
can be referred to</i>


00:41:45.922 --> 00:41:48.027
<i>as "the warrior tradition."</i>


00:41:48.027 --> 00:41:50.996
<i>Put simply, it's a ritual
performed to order.</i>


00:41:50.996 --> 00:41:52.686
<i>To make one a warrior,</i>


00:41:52.686 --> 00:41:55.931
<i>or to provide power
to that warrior.</i>


00:41:55.931 --> 00:42:00.005
<i>Sangomas have been
practicing</i> Muti <i>for centuries.</i>


00:42:04.836 --> 00:42:09.083
<i>Businessmen,
politicians, salesmen, you,</i>


00:42:09.083 --> 00:42:10.463
<i>anyone.</i>


00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:15.019
<i>People who pay
for</i> Muti <i>are seeking</i>


00:42:15.019 --> 00:42:16.780
<i>personal success,</i>


00:42:16.780 --> 00:42:17.885
<i>power,</i>


00:42:17.885 --> 00:42:19.576
<i>protection.</i>


00:42:19.576 --> 00:42:24.822
<i>They believe that</i> Muti
<i>strengthens their personal force,</i>


00:42:24.822 --> 00:42:26.306
<i>gives them an edge.</i>


00:42:29.896 --> 00:42:33.900
In <i>Muti,</i> specific body parts


00:42:33.900 --> 00:42:35.349
have a distinct effect.


00:42:35.349 --> 00:42:36.559
Mmm-hmm.


00:42:37.905 --> 00:42:39.389
Genitals,


00:42:39.389 --> 00:42:44.739
they bring virility, good luck.


00:42:44.739 --> 00:42:48.224
Especially if - they're virgin.
- Right.


00:42:48.224 --> 00:42:51.193
The eyes, farsightedness,


00:42:51.193 --> 00:42:52.643
clarity of vision.


00:42:53.057 --> 00:42:54.231
The brain,


00:42:55.094 --> 00:42:56.958
knowledge, political power.


00:42:56.958 --> 00:42:58.201
Mmm-hmm.


00:42:58.201 --> 00:43:01.099
The Sangoma takes
whatever they need


00:43:01.099 --> 00:43:02.273
for a specific outcome.


00:43:05.034 --> 00:43:07.659
- Jesus Christ.
- But, there's more.


00:43:09.246 --> 00:43:14.389
A Sangoman must take the flesh


00:43:14.389 --> 00:43:16.563
while the victim
is still alive...


00:43:16.563 --> 00:43:17.634
Right.


00:43:18.670 --> 00:43:20.878
In order to get the
power they seek...


00:43:20.878 --> 00:43:22.086
Mmm-hmm.


00:43:22.086 --> 00:43:24.123
...they must awaken
the gods to bestow it.


00:43:25.710 --> 00:43:27.056
Which means...


00:43:28.126 --> 00:43:29.887
the screams of the victim...


00:43:29.887 --> 00:43:31.268
Right.


00:43:31.268 --> 00:43:32.304
...are critical.


00:43:33.684 --> 00:43:36.065
The more intense the scream,


00:43:37.032 --> 00:43:39.172
the more powerful the <i>Muti.</i>


00:43:40.588 --> 00:43:45.766
Then the body parts are
mixed with the victim's blood,


00:43:46.628 --> 00:43:49.079
herbs, clay, gold,


00:43:49.079 --> 00:43:50.425
all of which is believed


00:43:50.425 --> 00:43:53.427
to attract and hold power.


00:43:55.327 --> 00:43:59.641
That elixir is drunk by
the client or the Sangoma,


00:44:00.539 --> 00:44:04.163
in order to get the
power they seek.


00:44:06.614 --> 00:44:08.753
They believe that it
turns them into a warrior.


00:44:08.753 --> 00:44:09.996
Makes them a warrior.


00:44:09.996 --> 00:44:11.619
And an undefeatable one.


00:44:13.344 --> 00:44:14.760
Sounds unbelievable to me.


00:44:15.829 --> 00:44:18.246
Right. To you, Detective.


00:44:18.246 --> 00:44:22.525
To him, it's simply
business. And very real.


00:44:23.181 --> 00:44:24.527
Very real.


00:44:27.324 --> 00:44:28.911
Whatever he's about to do,


00:44:30.775 --> 00:44:32.916
it feels he needs
power to do it.


00:44:32.916 --> 00:44:33.916
Mmm-hmm.


00:44:35.297 --> 00:44:36.298
And understand this.


00:44:37.887 --> 00:44:38.956
These first two,


00:44:40.199 --> 00:44:41.753
they were just
him getting ready.


00:44:42.891 --> 00:44:44.376
He did them for himself.


00:44:46.998 --> 00:44:48.000
<i>Capisce?</i>


00:44:52.246 --> 00:44:53.902
Do you really believe in this?


00:44:55.456 --> 00:44:58.389
Mmm-hmm. Yes.


00:45:01.634 --> 00:45:03.222
This is just too sick.


00:45:04.465 --> 00:45:08.123
I mean, Maria, it's sick
enough to be real, you know.


00:45:08.123 --> 00:45:10.367
I just wish I could see
this motherfucker's face.


00:45:13.853 --> 00:45:15.579
All I see right
now is a monster.


00:45:38.706 --> 00:45:41.570
I want one that's beautiful.
One with pretty eyes.


00:45:42.572 --> 00:45:47.163
One filled with
life and promise.


00:45:47.163 --> 00:45:49.371
Oh, I want her to have a
great deal of intelligence.


00:45:51.476 --> 00:45:54.548
And so much more to live for.


00:46:34.036 --> 00:46:35.003
Welcome.


00:46:37.557 --> 00:46:39.353
What can I - get for you?
- Tequila.


00:46:41.251 --> 00:46:42.666
Neat, or on the rocks?


00:46:42.666 --> 00:46:43.875
Neat. Okay.


00:46:48.327 --> 00:46:49.327
Are you new in town?


00:46:50.605 --> 00:46:51.606
Yes.


00:46:52.400 --> 00:46:53.746
Vacation?


00:46:53.746 --> 00:46:55.402
- No, work.
- Mmm.


00:46:56.507 --> 00:46:57.509
That's a really cool accent.


00:46:58.543 --> 00:46:59.579
I like it. Where is it from?


00:47:00.512 --> 00:47:02.478
I've been so many places.


00:47:02.478 --> 00:47:03.617
It is hard to say.


00:47:12.143 --> 00:47:13.456
May I be honest?


00:47:13.456 --> 00:47:14.490
Oh, sure.


00:47:15.907 --> 00:47:17.804
I like your eyes.


00:47:17.804 --> 00:47:18.943
Thank you.


00:47:20.393 --> 00:47:22.291
They are lovely. Stop it.


00:47:25.777 --> 00:47:26.987
I mean it.


00:47:26.987 --> 00:47:27.987
I really like them.


00:47:28.574 --> 00:47:29.574
Thank you.


00:47:30.300 --> 00:47:31.300
I really mean it, too.


00:47:34.822 --> 00:47:35.822
Hey.


00:47:38.860 --> 00:47:40.862
I could use eyes like that.


00:47:45.384 --> 00:47:46.454
My name is Randoku.


00:47:51.251 --> 00:47:52.219
What is your name?


00:47:53.391 --> 00:47:54.393
Randoku.


00:47:55.291 --> 00:47:56.291
I like that.


00:47:58.708 --> 00:47:59.708
I'm Terry.


00:48:02.539 --> 00:48:04.782
Tell me all about
yourself, Terry.


00:48:19.072 --> 00:48:20.833
This is just a
summer job for me.


00:48:21.972 --> 00:48:23.525
- You are in school?
- Yeah.


00:48:23.525 --> 00:48:25.182
Yeah. I'm pre-med
at the university.


00:48:25.942 --> 00:48:27.875
So, you are smart.


00:48:27.875 --> 00:48:29.911
I guess.


00:48:29.911 --> 00:48:33.121
This matches the van that was
reported stolen two weeks ago.


00:48:33.121 --> 00:48:34.123
Clear here?


00:48:35.641 --> 00:48:36.815
Yeah, it's clear here.


00:48:38.817 --> 00:48:41.474
Mmm, you wouldn't really know
it from meeting me in this place,


00:48:41.474 --> 00:48:44.512
but, I'm in the top one
percent of my class.


00:48:44.512 --> 00:48:46.237
I like that.


00:48:46.237 --> 00:48:47.860
Let's see if Terry
knows anything.


00:48:56.454 --> 00:48:58.077
Hey, Terry.
- Hey.


00:49:00.494 --> 00:49:02.737
Either of you wouldn't happen
to know anything about that van...


00:49:22.378 --> 00:49:23.688
<i>No, no. I get it.</i>


00:49:23.688 --> 00:49:26.244
It's a witch doctor
from Africa...


00:49:26.244 --> 00:49:27.623
Yeah, - that's right.
- And I should


00:49:27.623 --> 00:49:29.349
believe this because what?


00:49:29.349 --> 00:49:32.043
According to Dr. Mackles,
he's servicing a client.


00:49:33.836 --> 00:49:34.838
Hmm.


